@@doc """
Standard `Chainable` trait declaration.
`Chainable<$A, $Chained>` models chaining a contextual unary callable after a
contextual value. The `|>=` operator lowers through this trait.
The trait is intentionally not auto-imported because its helper name `chain`
would conflict with the existing `Result::chain` helper.
"""
deftrait Chainable<$A, $Chained> {
  # Chain a contextual callable after the contextual receiver.
  def chain(self: Self, f: ($A -> $Chained)) -> $Chained
}
